Error responses (thrown errors, 404s, returned responses with status >= 400) only receive headers staged on `event.res.errHeaders`. `setServerTiming()` only wrote to `event.res.headers`, so its entries were dropped from error responses,

- `setServerTiming()` now also writes to `event.res.errHeaders`, like the CORS utils do.
- `mergeHeaders()` now keeps both sides of `Server-Timing` (staged entries first, then the response's own) instead of replacing them. Without this, the change above would wipe a returned error response's own entries.

```ts
app.use((event) => setServerTiming(event, "auth", { dur: 1 }));
app.get("/fail", () => {
  throw new HTTPError({ status: 503, headers: { "server-timing": "upstream;dur=9" } });
});
// before: server-timing: upstream;dur=9
// after:  server-timing: auth;dur=1, upstream;dur=9
```

Used for nitrojs/nitro#4904

